findings.fix:
Define the rule: an account is dormant when clock.now - last_successful_login_at >= 30 x 24 h. last_successful_login_at is set at activation, and the rule is checked at sign-in as well as by the daily job. Rewrite the challenge:
- the last sign-in is at T0;
- a sign-in at T0+30d-1min succeeds and resets the clock;
- with no sign-in since T0, an attempt at T0+30d is refused with ACCOUNT_DORMANT;
- the job then writes iam.account.dormant exactly once.

State what happens to invited principals who never became active.
